  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_c21df1b8eeca418092c71a5c7f40a966",
      "statement": "Brijio's threat model assumes AI agents, networks, cloud infrastructure, and third-party services may be imperfect or untrusted, and rests on four core trust assumptions: the user explicitly starts and controls browser connections, authentication tokens are kept secret by authorized parties, the browser session belongs to the user, and the relay transports messages without requiring content inspection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/THREAT_MODEL.md#L4-L6",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2764ad2e50182467d6fb2ab96a676faddc329a18862874f5f6ece99d49c00e64:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/THREAT_MODEL.md#L58-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f631d289d658d40bca434b52ed9ebf9309f2fba350ff5bc3b1f30ff4c54bab9a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7ee7a8e753b74e0fb358c8b9c0a4da30",
      "statement": "The security goals are to protect browser sessions, avoid credential exposure, minimize unnecessary data transfer, reduce trust in relay infrastructure, and maintain user control.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/THREAT_MODEL.md#L8-L13",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:04d82b3fc72188bdc94c71600111ab9c3afd4fcaa707ba3330c28e846a817c18:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bf8f7ece54aa487d94645bf3629d8d49",
      "statement": "The threat model names four attacker classes — malicious agent, compromised relay, network attacker, and malicious website — whose mitigations are architectural: explicit request/response flows, no continuous streaming, user-controlled browser connections, progressive disclosure, TLS plus auth tokens, least-privilege extension permissions, and read-only structured content.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/THREAT_MODEL.md#L15-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d30cb2ebd88254777583c69bfd36cef7638f1e59523257b7d98b629ff5a823da:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e87bcb9ce30e4895b1381c9b87b4fd41",
      "statement": "TRUST_BOUNDARIES.md defines four trust boundaries: Agent↔MCP Server (MCP validates all requests and does not trust agent intent), MCP Server↔Brijio Relay (separate auth tokens, relay need not inspect payloads), Relay↔Browser Extension (pairing-token auth, extension does not trust relay for confidentiality), and Extension↔Browser Session (user-granted permissions, page data read as structured context never executed).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/TRUST_BOUNDARIES.md#L9-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6c4b8bc381b05c0241ae5e0b0f7fa16b59b39bca1ca85faf4a0a84503f52b5d7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6dba008c63e04406b0f01796155174b5",
      "statement": "The capability matrix marks cookie export, session cloning, browser mirroring, continuous screenshots, continuous DOM streaming, background surveillance, browser history collection, credential extraction, and MFA interception as intentionally unsupported product boundaries, not missing features; SECURITY_GUARANTEES.md adds that Brijio never exports cookies/passwords/passkeys/MFA codes and the browser session remains local.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/project/CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md#L165-L179",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3ff2bc6a02ced0ce2cc58656ad324db1996703ea2578b6e12c1958a13b98d5ab:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/SECURITY_GUARANTEES.md#L11-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:31c202c0e31a4bfd137b3c356c2a06c9d962cf3759863e6a6682ccb46cd33675:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dd9a538cf3064feb86cdfea91d3cdc23",
      "statement": "The no-continuous-screenshots non-goal is distinct from the bounded explicit capture_screenshot MCP tool (ADR 0064, Proposed), which is on-demand, viewport-only, active-tab JPEG capture via tabs.captureVisibleTab({format:'jpeg', quality:80}) with no auto-capture, background-tab capture, full-page scroll-stitch, or video.",
      "evidence": [
